ng and set the dependency to\n",[761,1125,1126],{},"nuxt-i18n-micro@3.21.4"," (or ",[761,1129,1130],{},"latest",") before installing.",[766,1133,1135],{"id":1134},"what-is-asserted","What is asserted",[744,1137,1138,1145],{},[755,1139,1142],{"href":1140,"rel":1141},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fs00d\u002Fnuxt-i18n-micro\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002Fscripts\u002Fsrc\u002Fcommands\u002Fsmoke-verify.ts",[759],[761,1143,1144],{},"scripts\u002Fsrc\u002Fcommands\u002Fsmoke-verify.ts","\ntakes a base URL, so the same checks run against a local server, a Cloudflare Pages\ndeployment or a Vercel one:",[1147,1148,1149,1168,1180],"ul",{},[1150,1151,1152,1155,1156,910,1158,910,1161,884,1164,1167],"li",{},[748,1153,1154],{},"SSR and localized routes"," — ",[761,1157,813],{},[761,1159,1160],{},"\u002Fde",[761,1162,1163],{},"\u002Ffr",[761,1165,1166],{},"\u002Fde\u002Fabout"," each render their own\ntranslations, interpolation and plurals resolve, and no page contains a raw\ntranslation key",[1150,1169,1170,1155,1173,1176,1177],{},[748,1171,1172],{},"Payload route",[761,1174,1175],{},"\u002F_locales\u002Findex\u002Fde\u002Fdata.json"," returns the right chunk and is not\nserved ",[761,1178,1179],{},"no-store",[1150,1181,1182,1155,1184,1187,1188,1191,1192,1195,1196,1199,1200,1203],{},[748,1183,77],{},[761,1185,1186],{},"hreflang"," for every locale plus ",[761,1189,1190],{},"x-default",", a ",[761,1193,1194],{},"canonical"," link, ",[761,1197,1198],{},"og:locale",",\nand ",[761,1201,1202],{},"\u003Chtml lang>"," matching the locale",[744,1205,1206,1213],{},[755,1207,1210],{"href":1208,"rel":1209},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fs00d\u002Fnuxt-i18n-micro\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002Fscripts\u002Fsrc\u002Fcommands\u002Fsmoke-browser.ts",[759],[761,1211,1212],{},"scripts\u002Fsrc\u002Fcommands\u002Fsmoke-browser.ts","\nadds what only a browser can see: hydration, client-side navigation between pages and\nlocales, that no raw key is ever visible mid-transition, and that nothing threw.",[766,1215,1217],{"id":1216},"deploying-from-ci","Deploying from CI",[744,1219,1220,1221,1224,1225,1228],{},"Deployment is off unless you tick ",[899,1222,1223],{},"deploy"," on a manual run. It always uses the\n",[748,1226,1227],{},"published"," package — the point is to verify what a user would get, and a local\ntarball would not survive the platform's own install step.",[744,1230,1231],{},"Create dedicated projects for this. Do not point it at a project you deploy by hand:\nevery run overwrites the deployment.",[1233,1234,1236],"h3",{"id":1235},"cloudflare-pages","Cloudflare Pages",[744,1238,1239,1242,1243,1247,1248,902,1251,1254,1255,1258,1259,1262,1263,1266],{},[748,1240,1241],{},"1. Create the project."," Open ",[755,1244,1245],{"href":1245,"rel":1246},"https:\u002F\u002Fdash.cloudflare.com",[759],", pick your account, then\n",[899,1249,1250],{},"Compute (Workers & Pages)",[748,1252,1253],{},"Create"," → the ",[748,1256,1257],{},"Pages"," tab → ",[748,1260,1261],{},"Upload assets",". Give it\na name — ",[761,1264,1265],{},"nuxt-i18n-micro-smoke"," — and drop in any file as a placeholder; CI replaces the\nwhole thing on its first run. A direct-upload project needs no Git connection, which is\nwhat you want here: the deploys come from this workflow, not from a branch.",[744,1268,1269,1270,1273],{},"The name you typed is the value for ",[761,1271,1272],{},"CLOUDFLARE_PROJECT_NAME",".",[744,1275,1276,1279],{},[748,1277,1278],{},"2. Account ID."," Look at the dashboard URL while inside the account:",[929,1281,1286],{"className":1282,"code":1284,"language":1285},[1283],"language-text","https:\u002F\u002Fdash.cloudflare.com\u002F8f1a2b3c4d5e6f7890abcdef12345678\u002Fworkers-and-pages\n                            └──────────── this is the account ID ────────────┘\n","text",[761,1287,1284],{"__ignoreMap":934},[744,1289,1290,1291,1294,1295,1273],{},"It is also printed in the right-hand sidebar of the Workers & Pages overview, under\n",[899,1292,1293],{},"Account details",". That value is ",[761,1296,1297],{},"CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID",[744,1299,1300,1303,1304,902,1308,1311,1312,902,1315,1273],{},[748,1301,1302],{},"3. API token."," Go to ",[755,1305,1306],{"href":1306,"rel":1307},"https:\u002F\u002Fdash.cloudflare.com\u002Fprofile\u002Fapi-tokens",[759],[748,1309,1310],{},"Create\nToken"," → scroll past the templates to ",[748,1313,1314],{},"Custom token",[748,1316,1317],{},"Get started",[744,1319,1320],{},"Fill it in like this:",[771,1322,1323,1333],{},[774,1324,1325],{},[777,1326,1327,1330],{},[780,1328,1329],{},"Field",[780,1331,1332],{},"What to put",[790,1334,1335,1346,1363,1374,1382],{},[777,1336,1337,1340],{},[795,1338,1339],{},"Token name",[795,1341,1342,1345],{},[761,1343,1344],{},"nuxt-i18n-micro smoke deploy"," — free text, only for you",[777,1347,1348,1351],{},[795,1349,1350],{},"Permissions",[795,1352,1353,1354,1357,1358,1357,1360],{},"one row: ",[748,1355,1356],{},"Account"," · ",[748,1359,1236],{},[748,1361,1362],{},"Edit",[777,1364,1365,1368],{},[795,1366,1367],{},"Account Resources",[795,1369,1370,1373],{},[748,1371,1372],{},"Include"," · the account you used in step 1",[777,1375,1376,1379],{},[795,1377,1378],{},"Client IP Address Filtering",[795,1380,1381],{},"leave empty — GitHub runners have no fixed IP",[777,1383,1384,1387],{},[795,1385,1386],{},"TTL",[795,1388,1389],{},"leave empty, or set an expiry date if you rotate tokens",[744,1391,1392,1394,1395,1398],{},[748,1393,1362],{}," rather than ",[748,1396,1397],{},"Read"," because the token has to create deployments, not just list\nthem. One permission row is enough — nothing here touches DNS or zones.",[744,1400,1401,1402,902,1405,1408,1409,1412,1413,1273],{},"Then ",[748,1403,1404],{},"Continue to summary",[748,1406,1407],{},"Create Token",". The token appears ",[748,1410,1411],{},"once",", on that\nscreen only. Copy it now; if you lose it, delete the token and make a new one. That value\nis ",[761,1414,1415],{},"CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN",[1233,1417,1419],{"id":1418},"vercel","Vercel",[744,1421,1422,1425,1426,1428],{},[748,1423,1424],{},"1. Create and link the project."," In ",[761,1427,763],{},", run:",[929,1430,1432],{"className":931,"code":1431,"language":933,"meta":934,"style":934},"pnpm dlx vercel link\n",[761,1433,1434],{"__ignoreMap":934},[938,1435,1436,1438,1441,1444],{"class":940,"line":353},[938,1437,951],{"class":950},[938,1439,1440],{"class":954}," dlx",[938,1442,1443],{"class":954}," vercel",[938,1445,1446],{"class":954}," link\n",[744,1448,1449,1450,1453,1454,1456,1457,1460,1461,1464],{},"It asks four things: which scope (your personal account, or a team if you have one),\nwhether to link to an existing project (answer ",[748,1451,1452],{},"no","), the project name\n(",[761,1455,1265],{},"), and the directory (press enter for ",[761,1458,1459],{},".\u002F","). This creates the\nproject on Vercel and writes ",[761,1462,1463],{},"test\u002Fdeploy-smoke\u002F.vercel\u002Fproject.json",":",[929,1466,1470],{"className":1467,"code":1468,"language":1469,"meta":934,"style":934},"language-json shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","{ \"orgId\": \"team_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\", \"projectId\": \"prj_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\" }\n","json",[761,1471,1472],{"__ignoreMap":934},[938,1473,1474,1477,1480,1484,1487,1489,1491,1494,1496,1499,1501,1504,1506,1508,1510,1513,1515],{"class":940,"line":353},[938,1475,1476],{"class":1013},"{",[938,1478,1479],{"class":1013}," \"",[938,1481,1483],{"class":1482},"spNyl","orgId",[938,1485,1486],{"class":1013},"\"",[938,1488,1464],{"class":1013},[938,1490,1479],{"class":1013},[938,1492,1493],{"class":954},"team_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",[938,1495,1486],{"class":1013},[938,1497,1498],{"class":1013},",",[938,1500,1479],{"class":1013},[938,1502,1503],{"class":1482},"projectId",[938,1505,1486],{"class":1013},[938,1507,1464],{"class":1013},[938,1509,1479],{"class":1013},[938,1511,1512],{"class":954},"prj_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",[938,1514,1486],{"class":1013},[938,1516,1517],{"class":1013}," }\n",[744,1519,1520,1521,1524,1525,1527,1528,1530,1531,884,1534,1537,1538,1540,1541,1544,1545,1273],{},"Newer CLI versions also write a ",[761,1522,1523],{},"projectName","; ignore it, nothing reads it. Only ",[761,1526,1483],{},"\nand ",[761,1529,1503],{}," matter — they become ",[761,1532,1533],{},"VERCEL_ORG_ID",[761,1535,1536],{},"VERCEL_PROJECT_ID",". ",[761,1539,1483],{},"\nstarts with ",[761,1542,1543],{},"team_"," for a team and is a plain user id for a personal account; copy either\nverbatim. The same pair is in the dashboard under ",[899,1546,1547],{},"Project Settings → General",[744,1549,1550,1556,1557,1560,1561,884,1563,1565,1566,1569],{},[748,1551,1552,1553,1273],{},"Do not commit ",[761,1554,1555],{},".vercel\u002F"," It is in ",[761,1558,1559],{},".gitignore"," already. CI never reads the file: with\n",[761,1562,1533],{},[761,1564,1536],{}," in the environment, ",[761,1567,1568],{},"vercel pull"," recreates it on\nthe runner. Locally the directory is only there to keep your own CLI linked — deleting it\nunlinks the directory and nothing else.",[744,1571,1572,1242,1575,902,1579,1273],{},[748,1573,1574],{},"2. Token.",[755,1576,1577],{"href":1577,"rel":1578},"https:\u002F\u002Fvercel.com\u002Faccount\u002Ftokens",[759],[748,1580,1407],{},[771,1582,1583,1591],{},[774,1584,1585],{},[777,1586,1587,1589],{},[780,1588,1329],{},[780,1590,1332],{},[790,1592,1593,1602,1613],{},[777,1594,1595,1598],{},[795,1596,1597],{},"Token Name",[795,1599,1600],{},[761,1601,1344],{},[777,1603,1604,1607],{},[795,1605,1606],{},"Scope",[795,1608,1609,1610],{},"the account or team that owns the project — this is where the ambiguity is: a personal token cannot deploy a team project, and vice versa. Pick the one whose name matches the scope you chose during ",[761,1611,1612],{},"vercel link",[777,1614,1615,1618],{},[795,1616,1617],{},"Expiration",[795,1619,1620],{},"your call; the workflow keeps working until it expires, then fails with a 403",[744,1622,1623,1624,1626,1627,1629,1630,1273],{},"Click ",[748,1625,1253],{},". The value is shown ",[748,1628,1411],{}," — that is ",[761,1631,1632],{},"VERCEL_TOKEN",[744,1634,1635,1636,1639,1640,1643,1644,1647],{},"Prefer the CLI? ",[761,1637,1638],{},"pnpm dlx vercel tokens add \"nuxt-i18n-micro smoke deploy\""," prints the\ntoken to stdout. Add ",[761,1641,1642],{},"--project prj_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"," to restrict it to this one\nproject, so a leak cannot touch anything else. Note that minting a token this way needs\nan existing account-scoped token — a fresh ",[761,1645,1646],{},"vercel login"," session cannot do it, so the\nfirst token has to come from the dashboard.",[1233,1649,1651],{"id":1650},"after-deploying","After deploying",[744,1653,1654],{},"CI waits for the new deployment to answer, then runs the same HTTP and browser checks\nagainst the live URL. A green deploy job means the published package works on that\nplatform's runtime — not just in a local Node server.",[744,1656,1657,1658,1661,1662,1273],{},"For ",[748,1659,1660],{},"local"," function\u002Fedge preset checks without deploying (Nitro-style vercel handler,\nwrangler, netlify serve), see ",[755,1663,505],{"href":506},[1665,1666,1667],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sHwdD, html code.shiki .sHwdD{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-default:#546E7A;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#676E95;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic}html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .s2Zo4, html code.shiki .s2Zo4{--shiki-light:#6182B8;--shiki-default:#82AAFF;--shiki-dark:#82AAFF}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-def